  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 143 AM EDT Fri May 29 2026\n\n- Quiet Weather into Next Week\n\nSurface high pressure and dry north flow will dominate the weather\nover the next week with no rain expected until the end of next\nweek. An Omega block will be across North America with Lower \nMichigan in between an upper high across central Canada and\ntroughing across eastern Canada into the NE CONUS. \n\nWeak frontal passages occur tonight and again Sunday night but \nthere is no moisture available until return flow sets up by next\nThursday. A cold front sagging down from the northwest could \nfocus showers and perhaps a thunderstorm Thursday night into \nSaturday before it clears Lower Michigan and high pressure builds\nin behind it.",
